# The development certificate is COMMITTED on purpose (devcert.pfx + devcert.cer), which is why
# the repository-wide "*.pfx" rule has to be overridden here.
#
# MSIX upgrades require an identical Publisher AND a package signed by a certificate the machine
# already trusts. A certificate regenerated per build would therefore break every existing install
# on the next release, and would change the .cer users were told to trust. One fixed identity is
# the correct behaviour.
#
# The consequence is deliberate and must be stated wherever it matters: this private key is public.
# Anyone can sign a package that Windows will call CN=AppPublisher. It authenticates the identity,
# not the publisher, and it is no substitute for a CA certificate (docs/packaging.md §5).
# Never treat a package signed with it as proof of official DlnRenderer provenance.
!devcert.pfx
